        <MovementNote>Light, graceful, and playful steps with coordinated hand gestures and turning motions</MovementNote>
        <ParticipantsNote>8–20 dancers; typically performed in mixed groups of boys and girls.</ParticipantsNote>
        <PerformedDuringNote>village festivals, feasts, and youth cultural programs.</PerformedDuringNote>
        <RegionalVariationNote>Minor differences in dance steps, costumes, and song lyrics among villages.</RegionalVariationNote>
        <SymbolismNote>Joy, beauty, romance, and communal harmony among the younger generation.</SymbolismNote>
        <TellsStoryOf>The hopes, emotions, and interactions of youth during festivals and social gatherings, marking celebration and social bonding.</TellsStoryOf>
        <hasSongNote>songs reflecting themes of youth, admiration, and courtship.</hasSongNote>
        <schema:description>cultural marker of identity for the Thadou-Kuki community.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


