        <FormationNote>Performed in rows or semi-circles, often in alternating sequences of men and women</FormationNote>
        <HistoricalOriginNote>evolved as a celebratory form of communal expression during harvest and festive occasions</HistoricalOriginNote>
        <MinCount rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</MinCount>
        <MovementNote>Simple, repetitive steps involving forward-backward motions, gentle swaying, clapping, and synchronized footwork in rhythm with the beat.</MovementNote>
        <MusicalInstrumentNote>a lively and rhythmic backdrop</MusicalInstrumentNote>
        <ParticipantsNote>2, 4 or Even Numbers</ParticipantsNote>
        <RegionalVariationNote>Minor variations in costume color, dance steps, and musical tempo depending on the village or clan.</RegionalVariationNote>
        <SymbolismNote>unity, cultural identity, prosperity, and the rhythm of community life</SymbolismNote>
        <TellsStoryOf>Unity, cultural identity, prosperity, and the rhythm of community life</TellsStoryOf>
        <schema:description>Commonest celebratory form of communal expression during harvest and festive occasions.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


