        <ParticipantsNote>6-12 dancers, sometimes more depending on the event;  typically performed by both young men and women.</ParticipantsNote>
        <PerformedDuringNote>Youth gatherings, festivals, post-harvest celebrations, and social nights in the lawm dormitory</PerformedDuringNote>
        <RegionalVariationNote>Slight differences in steps and dress styles between villages</RegionalVariationNote>
        <SymbolismNote>Discipline, cooperation, vitality, and social bonding among youth.</SymbolismNote>
        <TellsStoryOf>Youth training, unity, and celebration of communal life through the lawm institution, a traditional youth training and social system</TellsStoryOf>
        <schema:description>A youthful traditional dance performed as part of lawm institution (a traditional youth training and social system) activities, expressing joy, discipline, and group cohesion.</schema:description>
        <rdfs:comment>Yearly Celebration</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


