        <MusicalInstrumentNote>To keep a deep rhythmic beat.</MusicalInstrumentNote>
        <ParticipantsNote>Groups of 4–10; Primarily performed by hunters, women may join in celebration.</ParticipantsNote>
        <PerformedDuringNote>Post-hunt feasts, festivals, or when honoring a successful hunter.</PerformedDuringNote>
        <RegionalVariationNote>Some regions include fire-side storytelling with the dance.</RegionalVariationNote>
        <SymbolismNote>Courage, strength, provision, and thanksgiving to nature.</SymbolismNote>
        <TellsStoryOf>The triumph of hunters returning home with wild game, honoring bravery and teamwork in the hunt.</TellsStoryOf>
