        <linkedRitual rdf:resource="http://tk_tdo.org/ontologies/TK_TDO#Mim-Kut"/>
        <CostumeAttireNote>includes accessories like gun power pouch made of Mithun horn , feathers, or foliage.</CostumeAttireNote>
        <DanceInstrumentNote>Props imitating hunting gestures.</DanceInstrumentNote>
        <FormationNote>Line intermixing men and women forming circle with 2 couples in the center forming wild boar formation</FormationNote>
        <MinCount rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</MinCount>
        <MovementNote>Move in circle. Move sidwise in wave, dangling their knees.</MovementNote>
        <ParticipantsNote>Performed in even numbers (e.g., 8, 10, 12), usually in pairs.</ParticipantsNote>
        <RegionalVariationNote>Minor differences in dance patterns or center formation across clans.</RegionalVariationNote>
        <SymbolismNote>Dramatizing a wild boar hunt</SymbolismNote>
        <TellsStoryOf>Communal hunting, bravery, and unity in traditional village life.</TellsStoryOf>
        <schema:description>A seasonal dance dramatizing a wild boar hunt, performed during major agricultural festivals.</schema:description>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


