        <AssociatedDanceNote>dance focuses on symbolic movements</AssociatedDanceNote>
        <DanceInstrumentNote>None specific</DanceInstrumentNote>
        <FormationNote>Line or circular formation, often around a central altar or skull display.</FormationNote>
        <MinCount rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10</MinCount>
        <MovementNote>Slow, reverent steps with head tilts and circular motions; emphasis on symbolic gestures.</MovementNote>
        <ParticipantsNote>10 to 20</ParticipantsNote>
        <RegionalVariationNote>Varies in attire and musical tone across different clans</RegionalVariationNote>
        <SymbolismNote>Reverence for nature, ancestral rites, and valor in the hunt.</SymbolismNote>
        <TellsStoryOf>Honoring the spirit of the hunted animal and commemorating the hunter&apos;s bravery.</TellsStoryOf>
        <hasSongNote>Solemn chants or praise songs to ancestors and nature spirits</hasSongNote>
        <schema:description>A ritualistic dance centered on the ceremonial display of animal skulls, especially mithun (Guar or great Indian Bison) and deer.</schema:description>
        <rdfs:comment>After hunting mithun - funeral / farewell for mithun</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


