        <DurationNote>Short, embedded within a larger funerary sequence</DurationNote>
        <FoodPracticeNote>Ritual offering shared post-ritual</FoodPracticeNote>
        <GenderInclusivityNote>priestly role traditionally held</GenderInclusivityNote>
        <MusicalInstrumentNote>Occasional use for marking transitions</MusicalInstrumentNote>
        <ParticipantsNote>Priest (animist specialist), family, and spiritual agents (Chang Pathan, Noimangpa)</ParticipantsNote>
        <PerformedDuringNote>As part of the broader Thimit phot death ritual</PerformedDuringNote>
        <RegionalVariationNote>May differ in narrative and performance sequence</RegionalVariationNote>
        <SymbolismNote>Communal fulfillment (Sempet) of ancestral obligations; Release of the soul (Thilhah)</SymbolismNote>
        <TellsStoryOf>Journey of the deceased&apos;s spirit and responsibilities of the living to facilitate a peaceful afterlife.</TellsStoryOf>
        <hasSongNote>Ritual dialogue between Chang Pathan, Noimangpa, and the priest</hasSongNote>
        <schema:description>Ritual segment of the death rite ensuring the soul&apos;s proper transition to the ancestral realm.</schema:description>
        <schema:name>Thilhah le sempet</schema:name>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


